    },
    "body": "The completed pair search never proposed a correction of the earliest residual error: all 13,440 saved alternatives choose307 at position4 instead of267, including 4,146 gate-passing alternatives. Its selected960 coordinates nevertheless cover92.7977% of the focus term's available initial legal-descent estimate; only0.52525% of that estimate is aggregate-opposed at the focus-preferred destination. This weakens a simple ranking-omission explanation and does not justify widening the same sweep.\n\nThis adds source-bound saved-journal/gradient attribution, keeps the original report and a separate saturation-aware direction supplement, preserves exact sealed outputs and iCloud/runtime recovery receipts, and updates current-state. No new model score, proposal, gradient, fit or GPU job ran; accepted8/512 and unselected conditional6/15 and9/15 remain unchanged. Next is an optimistic fixed-state legal-pair mass bound against immutable Copy competition; that bound is NOT_RUN and a surviving bound would not establish feasibility.\n\nValidation: all546 input files freshly recovered and SHA-verified; normative Rust model/audit-root verification; complete frozen ranking match; actual-epoch CE/reference classification; ordered31-term f32 aggregate bit parity; independent parent scalar counts/potential calculation and specialist source/receipt review. Readers completed in2.7155s/190.9MB and0.9168s/92.8MB. Both derived roots exclusively claimed, sealed and fully verified. A tiny adapter compiles the unchanged normative report module; its2 existing tests pass. Named Rust formatting, Python syntax/JSON, claim wording and diff checks pass. The prior complete native arithmetic audit is reused, not rerun.\n\nAll evidence is retained in main and verified iCloud object codex-pair-proposal-attribution-20261009. Temporary branch/worktree, recovered inputs and dedicated adapter build will be removed after actual merge and fresh-main verification. References #2030.\n",
